  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Caden sold half of his comic books and then bought sixteen more. If he now has $36$, how many comic books did he have at the start?",
  "worked_solution": "Let $x=$ the number of comic books Caden had at the start.\n\nWe note that:\n\n- Half the number of comic books corresponds to $\\frac{1}{2}x.$\n\n- The number of comic books remaining after selling half of them corresponds to $x-\\frac{1}{2}x.$\n\n- The number of comic books remaining after selling half and buying sixteen more corresponds to $x-\\frac{1}{2}x+16.$\n\nThe final number of comic books is $36,$ so we have the equation\n\n$$\nx-\\frac{1}{2}x+16=36.\n$$\n\nWe can solve this equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{1}{2}x+16 & =36 \\\\ (1-\\frac{1}{2})x+16 & =36 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x+16 & =36 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x+16-16 & =36-16 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x & =20 \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x & =2\\cdot 20 \\\\ x & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, Caden had $40$ comic books at the start.",
